  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Empowering girls and women through education: a multidimensional approach</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This component works with the most disadvantaged rural girls in Malawi to provides mentorship, peer-to-peer learning and support, remedial education and life skills in the schools as well as in-kind support in forms of uniforms, shoes, sanitary pads and school supplies. It benefits 14,856 highly disadvantaged girls in upper primary directly with the goal to help them pass the primary exam and transitioning to secondary school, with the help of a mentor called &#x201C;learner guide&#x201D; who is a girl from the community who finished secondary school and serves as a role model. It also benefits an additional 386,644 girls and boys from the same schools through life skills curriculum.</narrative>
  </description>
